  "observedOutcome": "Active two-member groups now retain Active and the window count. Old production fails three active cases and passes two inactive/minimized cases; final production passes all five. Existing browser accessibility and original Quint switcher/focus gates pass. Native AT agrees with all actual taskbar control names and exactly one group toggle state; real pointer dismissal returns to the application and keyboard Home reaches the group. Native AT picker reopening then fails with WebKit termination and host exit 1.",
  "fixtureCorrections": [
    "Recognize native button alongside push button/toggle button without changing exact-name/count/state assertions.",
    "Preserve pointer application-return policy, then exercise keyboard opener-return using real Super+Alt+Space, application dismissal and Home/arrow navigation. Match immutable group control identity rather than its changing state label. Original deadlines and final bar-opener/Orca agreement assertions are unchanged."
  ],
  "modelScope": "Projection-only Surface detail change; no reducer, admission or effect-authority change. Existing explicitly selected switcher/focus Quint tests and sampled invariants pass; these do not prove native AT behavior. No new model created for text/state projection.",
  "missingObservations": [
    "Complete native picker action/return and remaining original AT journey are unverified: WebKit terminated during reopening under AT inspection.",
    "Native speech/braille semantic oracle, per-control native actions and independent acceptance remain open.",
    "No core stack is available: kernel records RLIMIT_CORE=1 aborting the dump; no OOM event found in the bounded crash interval."
  ],
